  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find $Ha$ if\n$H=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$a=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $Ha=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ha=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot 7+2\\cdot 3 \\\\ \u2217\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ \u2217\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ha=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ -3\\cdot 7+6\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$Ha=[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$",
